  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "The aorta is located in the chest, and it is the largest artery in the
    body. It begins at the heart and rises up before arching back down through the
    chest and into the abdomen. \n\nThe aorta's main job is to carry oxygen-rich
    blood from the heart and distribute it to the rest of the body. It starts from
    the left ventricle of the heart and then travels upward (this part is called
    the ascending aorta), arches (the aortic arch), and goes down through the chest
    and into the abdomen (where it becomes the descending aorta).\r\n\r\nIt's important
    to know where the aorta is and how it functions because problems with this artery,
    such as blockages or aneurysms, can significantly affect blood flow throughout
    the body. \n\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
