  m_text: "In addition to chest or back pain, someone with an aortic aneurysm might
    also experience other symptoms like pain in the abdomen, difficulty breathing,
    or a rapid heartbeat. It\u2019s important to recognize these signs because a
    ruptured aortic aneurysm can lead to life-threatening bleeding.\r\n\r\nIf someone
    experiences this type of pain, especially if it's sudden and severe, it is crucial
    to seek immediate medical attention. Understanding these warning signs can help
    you act quickly and save a life, as early intervention is critical for the best
    outcomes"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
